// A stray `{` in a string literal (meant as a literal brace) opens an
// interpolation that never closes: the `}` of the enclosing block is consumed
// as its close, then the string runs to EOF. The lexer reports at the offending
// brace with a message naming interpolation and the `\{` escape (design 119
// Part C, closing DF-116d), not a far-off "unterminated string" at EOF.
// EXPECT: error
// EXPECT-ERROR-CONTAINS: unterminated interpolation in string literal

func main() {
    let msg = "value {x"
    print(msg)
}
